@name Spanish speaker of English
@about Five pure vowels, no θ ð z or ʃ in the usual places, and a vowel in front of word-initial s clusters ("eschool").
@rhythm syllable
@strip length
# Diphthongs first, before their parts change on their own.
o ʊ > o
e ɪ > e i
# Spanish has five vowels, so English's many vowels collapse onto them.
ɪ > i
ʊ > u
ə > e
æ > a
ʌ > a
ɜ > e
ɑ > a
ɒ > o
ɔ > o
ɛ > e
# Consonants English has and Spanish lacks.
θ > s
ð > d
z > s
v > b
ʃ > t͡ʃ
d͡ʒ > ʝ
h > x / # _
ɹ > r / # _
ɹ > ɾ
# A word cannot begin with s + consonant, so Spanish speakers add an e.
∅ > e / # _ s {p,t,k}
